{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "28", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "10", "S": "53"}}, "news": [{"title": "BMC panel to decide fate of 3,169 trees for Dharavi redevelopment & infrastructure projects in Mumbai", "para": "Mumbai's Tree Authority will consider proposals impacting 3,169 trees on Tuesday.  Permissions are sought to fell 1,777 trees and transplant 1,392 others for development.  The Dharavi redevelopment project seeks to remove 1,693 trees, with compensatory planting planned.  Other projects include a tunnel, IIT housing, and a slum rehabilitation scheme.  These decisions come amid growing scrutiny over tree removal for infrastructure.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/bmc-panel-to-decide-fate-of-3169-trees-for-dharavi-redevelopment-infrastructure-projects-in-mumbai/132675022?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-2067273/132675022.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Mumbai: BMC panel to consider leasing 15-acre Mulund dump land for Dharavi redevelopment works", "para": "The BMC plans to lease fifteen acres of reclaimed land at Mulund dumping ground. This land will be used by Dharavi Redevelopment Project for a casting yard. The civic body expects to earn over one hundred crore rupees in rent. The developer will manage site remediation and obtain necessary environmental clearances. This proposal will soon be presented for approval by the Improvement Committee.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/mumbai-bmc-panel-to-consider-leasing-15-acre-mulund-dump-land-for-dharavi-redevelopment-works/132674995?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1958840/132674995.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Telangana grants special relaxation for commercial high-rise in Jubilee Hills", "para": "Hyderabad government approved special concessions for a commercial building construction.  The high-rise will be permitted extra height and other building rule relaxations.  This special case allows construction up to thirty meters with additional floors.  Applicants will surrender land for road widening free of cost.  The order follows examination of representations and municipal reports.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/telangana-approves-new-high-rise-commercial-building-in-jubilee-hills-with-special-relaxation/132674612?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1487990/132674612.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}]}